(5692160, 828288, 100393, '<td valign="top">Great landscape image which would probably do well in a FS. Enough negative space for a movie poster. I think the title is a bit of a push on the feasibility stakes and the red sky is sufficiently well coloured that some other-wordly title may have worked.....<br/> <br/>Perhaps something like: ''Destination Planet Chronos''?<br/> <br/>Image is good enough to squeeze a 7 out of me.</td>', 'Great landscape image which would probably do well in a FS. Enough negative space for a movie poster. I think the title is a bit of a push on the feasibility stakes and the red sky is sufficiently well coloured that some other-wordly title may have worked..... Perhaps something like: ''Destination Planet Chronos''? Image is good enough to squeeze a 7 out of me.', '2009-10-19 10:44:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5692163, 828227, 100393, '<td valign="top">I think the title stretches movie title credibility and though the picture is pretty good - it doesn''t say ''movie'' to me in the same way as some of the other entries do.<br/> <br/>It is a well executed image though and I do like that you have left plenty of negative space like many movie posters have.</td>', 'I think the title stretches movie title credibility and though the picture is pretty good - it doesn''t say ''movie'' to me in the same way as some of the other entries do. It is a well executed image though and I do like that you have left plenty of negative space like many movie posters have.', '2009-10-19 10:46:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(5692164, 828159, 100393, '<td valign="top">Not a bad title (but not great either) but with  an excellent photographic realisation of your chosen vision.<br/> <br/>I''m liking the faithful aspect ration and the negative space for graphics.<br/> <br/>Photographically, this is pretty impressive and probably much harder than it looks. I hope to see this on the front page; I''m not sure it will have wide enough appeal - but I hope so.</td>', 'Not a bad title (but not great either) but with  an excellent photographic realisation of your chosen vision. I''m liking the faithful aspect ration and the negative space for graphics. Photographically, this is pretty impressive and probably much harder than it looks. I hope to see this on the front page; I''m not sure it will have wide enough appeal - but I hope so.', '2009-10-19 10:50:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5692165, 828368, 100393, '<td valign="top">Wow - out of the box (by quite a margin) - I like that. Title is credible enough and the image communicates the vision in the title.<br/> <br/>Photographically - very brave and i''m sure you''ve pulled off the look that you were after. Does it look like a movie poster? Kind of - yes.<br/> <br/>Good job.</td>', 'Wow - out of the box (by quite a margin) - I like that. Title is credible enough and the image communicates the vision in the title. Photographically - very brave and i''m sure you''ve pulled off the look that you were after. Does it look like a movie poster? Kind of - yes. Good job.', '2009-10-19 10:53:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5692169, 828338, 100393, '<td valign="top">Nearly a good title - but the last word seems a bit pushed. Might have been worth getting some kind of goblet in there and going for ''Dalaman''s Poison Chalice''.<br/> <br/>Very nicely lit image though - compositionally I think I would have had the snake slightly lower in the frame, but hey, what do I know.<br/> <br/>Overall, pretty good though.</td>', 'Nearly a good title - but the last word seems a bit pushed. Might have been worth getting some kind of goblet in there and going for ''Dalaman''s Poison Chalice''. Very nicely lit image though - compositionally I think I would have had the snake slightly lower in the frame, but hey, what do I know. Overall, pretty good though.', '2009-10-19 10:59:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(5692172, 828202, 100393, '<td valign="top">Interesting title - I think ''catastrophe'' rather than ''calamity'' might have suited your brooding image a little better.<br/> <br/>I actually think a portrait orientation with plenty of negative space above would have worked really well with this.<br/> <br/>Overall, I like the image quite a lot but I think it struggles a little as a movie poster.</td>', 'Interesting title - I think ''catastrophe'' rather than ''calamity'' might have suited your brooding image a little better. I actually think a portrait orientation with plenty of negative space above would have worked really well with this. Overall, I like the image quite a lot but I think it struggles a little as a movie poster.', '2009-10-19 11:01:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5692193, 828066, 89230, '<td valign="top">This photo struggles with the same thing that I often have a challenge with in my photography: halos. There is an OK tutorial in the learning section of DPC, but for me it is still something I am trying to work on. <br/> <br/>I like the idea, and the subject.</td>', 'This photo struggles with the same thing that I often have a challenge with in my photography: halos. There is an OK tutorial in the learning section of DPC, but for me it is still something I am trying to work on.  I like the idea, and the subject.', '2009-10-19 11:41:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(5692194, 828047, 89230, '<td valign="top">What a fantastic idea. I like it. At first glance it isnt quite straight (rotation wise), but it might just be the angle and architecture.</td>', 'What a fantastic idea. I like it. At first glance it isnt quite straight (rotation wise), but it might just be the angle and architecture.', '2009-10-19 11:43:02.000000', NULL, 1),
