(5706039, 828160, 31637, '<td valign="top">I''m glad you ribboned now, this is a fabulous piece of art, well deserved podium finish; thanks for the description and photo details.</td>', 'I''m glad you ribboned now, this is a fabulous piece of art, well deserved podium finish; thanks for the description and photo details.', '2009-10-29 21:14:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(5706053, 827776, 77196, '<td valign="top">A world-class image, capturing a great moment, expressing great emotion, telling a story, and you, yes you did it. The quality was recognized by over 125 of some of the harshest critics in the world - many of whom had personal reasons to grade you down so they could do better (hold the fire - not saying people do, just that they have reason to...). Even without the validation of the others, this is an image you can be proud of for years to come. The DQ has absolutely no impact on the quality of the image. Plus, now you KNOW that YOU can get a blue ribbon on DPC. So sorry about the DQ, but the image is worth celebrating all in its own right. <br/></td>', 'A world-class image, capturing a great moment, expressing great emotion, telling a story, and you, yes you did it. The quality was recognized by over 125 of some of the harshest critics in the world - many of whom had personal reasons to grade you down so they could do better (hold the fire - not saying people do, just that they have reason to...). Even without the validation of the others, this is an image you can be proud of for years to come. The DQ has absolutely no impact on the quality of the image. Plus, now you KNOW that YOU can get a blue ribbon on DPC. So sorry about the DQ, but the image is worth celebrating all in its own right. ', '2009-10-29 21:42:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(5706054, 828279, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: Menacing b/w of the hills and sky behind, which only seems to play up the lack of similar varied tones in the Phantom.  Had to look for the blade.<br/> <br/>Technical: Great light, good use of thirds, nice dof...though a 30-second exposure seems a little long!  I think that a lesser exposure, esp with the phantom in the pic, would have resulted in a more multi-tonal and powerful image.<br/> <br/>Aristic: Frankly I thought Phantom looked cut-and-paste and posed.  However you placed in the top 20 in this challenge, so can''t argue with that :-)<br/> <br/>Overall: Great concept, I just feel execution could have been a little stronger to make the phantom more menacing.  good work!<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: Menacing b/w of the hills and sky behind, which only seems to play up the lack of similar varied tones in the Phantom.  Had to look for the blade. Technical: Great light, good use of thirds, nice dof...though a 30-second exposure seems a little long!  I think that a lesser exposure, esp with the phantom in the pic, would have resulted in a more multi-tonal and powerful image. Aristic: Frankly I thought Phantom looked cut-and-paste and posed.  However you placed in the top 20 in this challenge, so can''t argue with that :-) Overall: Great concept, I just feel execution could have been a little stronger to make the phantom more menacing.  good work! Feel free to PM me with any questions, Susan', '2009-10-29 21:42:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(5706058, 828262, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: Very realistic, almost scarily so.  Glad to see I wasn''t the only one :-)<br/> <br/>Technical: Great use of ambient lighting, dof a little shallow - would have loved to see more of the face in focus esp the lips and lower eye. I voted this a 7 during voting, for the one eye in focus is quite vivid and real...but the rest was oof. The high shutter speed and ISO seems to indicate a handheld shot; with a tripod may have been able to take more time and get the DOF. Do like the oof leaves in foreground, add trememdous depth and realism and a time of season.  Could be a book cover.<br/> <br/>Artistic: Huge kudos to the model for a great look and not flinching/blinking!  She is very convincing as a corpse. Having been a model, I know very well how difficult work like this can be. Hope she got a nice big mug of coffee or hot chocolate afterwards!<br/> <br/>Overall: Disapppointed at the low finish, I expected a top 20 finish at least. Still, an excellent idea, and great work!<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: Very realistic, almost scarily so.  Glad to see I wasn''t the only one :-) Technical: Great use of ambient lighting, dof a little shallow - would have loved to see more of the face in focus esp the lips and lower eye. I voted this a 7 during voting, for the one eye in focus is quite vivid and real...but the rest was oof. The high shutter speed and ISO seems to indicate a handheld shot; with a tripod may have been able to take more time and get the DOF. Do like the oof leaves in foreground, add trememdous depth and realism and a time of season.  Could be a book cover. Artistic: Huge kudos to the model for a great look and not flinching/blinking!  She is very convincing as a corpse. Having been a model, I know very well how difficult work like this can be. Hope she got a nice big mug of coffee or hot chocolate afterwards! Overall: Disapppointed at the low finish, I expected a top 20 finish at least. Still, an excellent idea, and great work! Feel free to PM me with any questions, Susan', '2009-10-29 21:55:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(5706063, 828141, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: Basically a really promising shot, but the lack of tones is probably why I voted this a 6 during voting.<br/> <br/>Technical: Good use of dof and thirds; like the overhang of the tree leading you to the circle. Have to admit though the image as is leaves me feeling a little flat, like there is more going on that we are missing. <br/> <br/>Artistic: Given such an ancient and yes, likely pagan symbol, I would have liked to see a more dramatic presentation of same.  Perhaps imagine yourself as a fearful peasant from yonks ago, stumbling across this image as the light fell...you may have fallen to your knees in worship/fear/both!  <br/> <br/>Overall/FWIW: If only for fun, and if feasible (the UK is a small enough island), try shooting this scene again from different heights.  I probably would''ve been on my back or tummy, as I tend to like shooting extreme POV.<br/> <br/>Having said that, you finished quite well, so keep shooting and good luck!<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: Basically a really promising shot, but the lack of tones is probably why I voted this a 6 during voting. Technical: Good use of dof and thirds; like the overhang of the tree leading you to the circle. Have to admit though the image as is leaves me feeling a little flat, like there is more going on that we are missing.  Artistic: Given such an ancient and yes, likely pagan symbol, I would have liked to see a more dramatic presentation of same.  Perhaps imagine yourself as a fearful peasant from yonks ago, stumbling across this image as the light fell...you may have fallen to your knees in worship/fear/both!   Overall/FWIW: If only for fun, and if feasible (the UK is a small enough island), try shooting this scene again from different heights.  I probably would''ve been on my back or tummy, as I tend to like shooting extreme POV. Having said that, you finished quite well, so keep shooting and good luck! Feel free to PM me with any questions, Susan', '2009-10-29 22:05:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(5706067, 828108, 63218, '<td valign="top">I keep thinking how does the ''3rd rail'' deal w/all that standing water? Wow.</td>', 'I keep thinking how does the ''3rd rail'' deal w/all that standing water? Wow.', '2009-10-29 22:10:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(5706069, 828317, 105079, '<td valign="top">This is f''ing rad.  It affects the viewer.</td>', 'This is f''ing rad.  It affects the viewer.', '2009-10-29 22:12:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(5706076, 828266, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>*scratching head* compression artifacts?  Where, Spiffy? *ahem* now on with the critique...<br/> <br/>Initial impression: Very simple, powerful image.  Less is more and it definitely works here. I voted quickly, which is probably why I only gave it a 6.  Now, looking at it more, it warrants a 7.<br/> <br/>Technical: Great setting, great thirds, nice murky image which offsets the flat blackness of the bulk of the figure...as has been noted already, as though a human has been cut out of the image.  Deliberate or not, it works very well.  Surprised at your settings - very shallow DOF, very high ISO and shutter speed.  But it works.<br/> <br/>Artistic: The note in hand makes me wonder if it is a summons of sorts.  Wow, there really is a Loch Lomond?! I thought it was just a fictitous brand of whisky drunk by Captain Haddock in the Tintin series :-)  And yes, the effective negative space does draw the eye to the person.  Didn''t even notice the not-perfectly level horizon until it was pointed out, which may help add to an unsettling feel.<br/> <br/>Overall: Very well done image, quiet but menacing at the same time.  What will the note tell the person to do?<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! *scratching head* compression artifacts?  Where, Spiffy? *ahem* now on with the critique... Initial impression: Very simple, powerful image.  Less is more and it definitely works here. I voted quickly, which is probably why I only gave it a 6.  Now, looking at it more, it warrants a 7. Technical: Great setting, great thirds, nice murky image which offsets the flat blackness of the bulk of the figure...as has been noted already, as though a human has been cut out of the image.  Deliberate or not, it works very well.  Surprised at your settings - very shallow DOF, very high ISO and shutter speed.  But it works. Artistic: The note in hand makes me wonder if it is a summons of sorts.  Wow, there really is a Loch Lomond?! I thought it was just a fictitous brand of whisky drunk by Captain Haddock in the Tintin series :-)  And yes, the effective negative space does draw the eye to the person.  Didn''t even notice the not-perfectly level horizon until it was pointed out, which may help add to an unsettling feel. Overall: Very well done image, quiet but menacing at the same time.  What will the note tell the person to do? Feel free to PM me with any questions, Susan', '2009-10-29 22:17:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(5706119, 827776, 68504, '<td valign="top">VERY cunning picture and entry.  (Alas, one of the many reasons I mostly just do stuff in Irfanview: rotation does not affect the original file.  Probably a good opportunity to fine tune your workflow, as Chromedome suggests.  But hey, this was a big victory, not least in getting dpc voters to appreciate a fine piece of work).</td>', 'VERY cunning picture and entry.  (Alas, one of the many reasons I mostly just do stuff in Irfanview: rotation does not affect the original file.  Probably a good opportunity to fine tune your workflow, as Chromedome suggests.  But hey, this was a big victory, not least in getting dpc voters to appreciate a fine piece of work).', '2009-10-29 23:29:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(5706124, 827776, 34659, '<td valign="top">I hope this is re-instated.  However, regardless of the final verdict, this is a fantastic image and worthy of the blue.  We all know you didn''t "cheat" or "intentionally bypass the rules".<br/> <br/>Keep up the great work and we''ll see you on the front page again soon!  Lotsa hugs &amp; congratulations on a fantastic job!!!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-10-29 23:37:47.</i></td>', 'I hope this is re-instated.  However, regardless of the final verdict, this is a fantastic image and worthy of the blue.  We all know you didn''t "cheat" or "intentionally bypass the rules". Keep up the great work and we''ll see you on the front page again soon!  Lotsa hugs & congratulations on a fantastic job!!!', '2009-10-29 23:37:20.000000', '2009-10-29 23:37:47.000000', 0),
